snapshot/.planning/phases/46-ci-load-shape-and-operator-input-validation/46-02-PLAN.md:328:| T-46-06 | Tampering | `git check-ref-format` argv in `ensure_base_is_a_local_branch` | high | mitigate | Pass the already-qualified `refs/heads/{base}` string, never the raw value. Measured: a raw base of `-x` is parsed as a FLAG and yields exit 129, while `refs/heads/-x` is never option-shaped and yields exit 0. Both calls reuse one `qualified` binding so the two can never diverge. Enforced by acceptance criterion "the raw `base` is passed to neither". |
snapshot/.planning/phases/46-ci-load-shape-and-operator-input-validation/46-02-PLAN.md-329-| T-46-07 | Tampering / Elevation of Privilege | validator-versus-consumer ref spelling (R-01) | medium | accept | A value that is both a legal literal ref name and a revision expression (`@`) passes validation and then forks from HEAD rather than from the branch. PRE-EXISTING — today's `rev-parse` path prefixes `refs/heads/` too — and unchanged by D-07. Requires the operator to deliberately configure an exotic base AND to have created a branch under that name. Closing it needs the validator and consumer to agree on one spelling, a devflow-core change explicitly outside this phase's boundary. Accepted here, surfaced at phase close so the filing decision is made deliberately rather than by silence. |
