snapshot/.planning/milestones/v2.3.0-phases/31-claude-adapter-launch-path-pipe-owning-monitor-999-64-arc-cl/31-02-PLAN.md-359-|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
snapshot/.planning/milestones/v2.3.0-phases/31-claude-adapter-launch-path-pipe-owning-monitor-999-64-arc-cl/31-02-PLAN.md-360-| T-31-06 | Repudiation | `evaluate_layer1` ordering | high | mitigate | The idle-timeout verdict is read as the first statement of `evaluate_layer1`, before `read_capture` and before `parse_claude_event_result`. Appending it to the stdout capture instead would leave it unreachable on any stream that already contained a `result` event — the real outcome would go unrecorded and a stale success would stand. The regression fixture carries a prior real `result` event and a negative control. |
snapshot/.planning/milestones/v2.3.0-phases/31-claude-adapter-launch-path-pipe-owning-monitor-999-64-arc-cl/31-02-PLAN.md:361:| T-31-07 | Elevation of Privilege | process-group termination | high | mitigate | Signals are sent against the in-memory `Child` handle's own group id, never against the on-disk `phase-NN-agent-pid` file, which is exposed to pid reuse. `agent::agent_running`/`terminate_and_verify` are reused for the liveness re-check rather than an ad-hoc `/proc` parse, because they already handle the `pid <= 0` and `kill(-1, ...)` hazards this crate has been bitten by. |
snapshot/.planning/milestones/v2.3.0-phases/31-claude-adapter-launch-path-pipe-owning-monitor-999-64-arc-cl/31-02-PLAN.md-362-| T-31-08 | Denial of Service | `parse_idle_timeout_secs` | medium | mitigate | A configured value below the floor is clamped to 30 seconds so a mis-set environment cannot terminate healthy runs — a 12-second bound would have killed a live healthy run in 2 of 7 measured trials. The clamp is reported to the caller as a value and logged loudly in the parent process where the operator can see it, never silently in a detached process whose stdio is null. |
snapshot/.planning/milestones/v2.3.0-phases/31-claude-adapter-launch-path-pipe-owning-monitor-999-64-arc-cl/31-02-PLAN.md-363-| T-31-09 | Tampering | commit enumeration on timeout | medium | mitigate | The firing sequence reads the commit log and never writes to it. No rollback, reset, or revert is permitted: a timeout may be a false positive, and destroying real work on a false positive is unrecoverable. `idle_timeout_does_not_roll_back_commits` asserts the count is unchanged. |
